FOV=VFOV=90, 512x512 -\\u003e f=256px. Horizon v=256.\\nGround point from pixel (u,v): d = 1.55*256/(v-256) [along optical axis],\\n lateral = (u-256)*d/256. Then rotate by camera heading.\\n\\n## obs_0001 (pose: (0,0), heading 0deg = +y)\\n- potted plant, small tree in cylindrical pot: u78,v370 -\\u003e cam(-2.42, 3.48)\\n- wooden chair (back visible, facing ~right): u145,v322 -\\u003e cam(-2.61, 6.01)\\n- small wooden table (square top, 4 legs): u222,v330 -\\u003e cam(-0.71, 5.36)\\n- large white/gray box, counter-like (long, axis ~ +y): near corner (340,450) d2.05 x0.67; far corner (305,355) d4.01 x0.77 -\\u003e center ~(0.9,3.0)\\n- gray couch/sofa-ish object behind counter, partly occluded: u320-415, v275-310. depth unresolved\\n- dark small box on top/behind counter at u325,v290 (maybe part of sofa/armrest)\\n- wooden bench w/ tall back (right): legs u455,v360 -\\u003e cam(2.97, 3.82)\\nBack wall bright/overexposed. Left \\u0026 right walls visible.\\nEOF\\ncat \\u003e /work/geo.py \\u003c\\u003c 'EOF'\\nimport math,sys,json\\nF=256.0; H=1.55; C=256.0\\ndef g(u,v,px=0.0,py=0.0,hd=0.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"pixel -\\u003e world ground xy. hd = camera heading in deg, clockwise from +y.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if v\\u003c=C+0.5: return None\\n    d=H*C/(v-C)            # forward along optical axis\\n    lat=(u-C)*d/C          # right of camera\\n    a=math.radians(hd)\\n    # heading hd clockwise from +y: forward=(sin a, cos a); right=(cos a, -sin a)\\n    x=px+d*math.sin(a)+lat*math.cos(a)\\n    y=py+d*math.cos(a)-lat*math.sin(a)\\n    return round(x,2),round(y,2),round(d,2)\\nif __name__==\\\"__main__\\\":\\n    for arg in sys.argv[1:]:\\n        p=[float(t) for t in arg.split(\\\",\\\")]\\n        print(arg,\\\"-\\u003e\\\",g(*p))\\nEOF\\necho ok\",\"description\":\"Write initial notes with geometry helper\"}"}},{"type":"content_block_stop","index":2},{"type":"message_delta","delta":{"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null},"usage":{"input_tok